# The relay's HTTPS front (docs/self-hosting.md). Caddy gets a certificate for RELAY_DOMAIN and
# renews it on its own, and redirects plain HTTP to HTTPS.
#
# There is no `log` directive on purpose: without one Caddy keeps no access log, so no IP
# addresses are written down, which is what the relay promises (relay/README.md).
# Nothing else is needed: Caddy waits as long as the relay's 25-second long polls take, and the
# relay sets its own CORS and caching headers.
{$RELAY_DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy relay:8080
}
